# Impeccable Core Rules

This defines the quality standard for all UI.

Impeccable is not about decoration.
It is about clarity, intention, and effortless experience.

---

## Core Principle

Everything must feel natural, clear, and easy to use.

If something feels confusing, heavy, or forced → it is not impeccable.

---

## Clarity

- The user must immediately understand:
  - what this screen is
  - what they can do
- Avoid ambiguity
- Avoid unnecessary complexity

---

## Effortless

- The UI should feel easy to use without thinking
- Navigation should be obvious
- Actions should be intuitive
- Reduce cognitive load

---

## Intentional Design

- Every element must have a purpose
- No random:
  - colors
  - spacing
  - shadows
- Always ask: "Why does this exist?"

---

## Invisible Design

- The UI should not draw attention to itself
- Focus on content and experience
- Avoid over-styling

---

## No Friction

- Remove all small annoyances:
  - poor contrast
  - tight spacing
  - unclear buttons
  - broken images
- Ensure smooth experience everywhere

---

## Quality over Quantity

- Prefer fewer, better components
- Avoid adding unnecessary features
- Focus on refining what exists

---

## Implementation Constraints

- Do not change business logic
- Do not break existing features
- Keep UI simple and readable
- Maintain consistency across components

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- clear
- calm
- effortless
- intentional
- high quality
